WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.270 --> 00:00:06.090
Gunshots echo down the concrete hallway of
Site-22.

00:00:06.090 --> 00:00:08.420
Screams are the only thing that escape each
room.

00:00:08.420 --> 00:00:13.209
A team of men in all black combat gear and
masks move from one section of the complex

00:00:13.209 --> 00:00:14.209
to the next.

00:00:14.209 --> 00:00:18.880
Pietro Wilson hides in his office, listening
to the cries for mercy of his colleagues.

00:00:18.880 --> 00:00:21.610
He shakes uncontrollably with fear.

00:00:21.610 --> 00:00:23.090
Who are they? he thinks.

00:00:23.090 --> 00:00:26.340
Why are they killing everyone and how did
they find us?

00:00:26.340 --> 00:00:30.230
Moments earlier Pietro Wilson had been in
the canteen eating dinner with other staff

00:00:30.230 --> 00:00:31.230
members.

00:00:31.230 --> 00:00:33.190
A group of heavily armed men entered the room.

00:00:33.190 --> 00:00:35.830
They stood silently surveying the area.

00:00:35.830 --> 00:00:38.610
One of the scientists stood up and asked if
they could assist them.

00:00:38.610 --> 00:00:40.510
That’s when the carnage started.

00:00:40.510 --> 00:00:44.200
One of the masked men raised his rifle and
shot the scientists in the head.

00:00:44.200 --> 00:00:48.510
Chaos broke out as the other mercenaries raised
their weapons and began firing.

00:00:48.510 --> 00:00:52.760
Bullets flew everywhere and Pietro was lucky
not to be struck or trampled as he escaped

00:00:52.760 --> 00:00:54.720
out the back door of the cafeteria.

00:00:54.720 --> 00:00:59.079
He ran to his office, slammed the door shut,
and hid under his desk.

00:00:59.079 --> 00:01:04.610
Now he sits on the floor with his legs pulled
up to his chest shaking uncontrollably.

00:01:04.610 --> 00:01:09.530
After a couple of minutes he manages to take
a deep breath and slows his heart rate.

00:01:09.530 --> 00:01:14.409
He regains control of his body, but is still
filled with fear and adrenaline.

00:01:14.409 --> 00:01:16.929
Pietro crawls on his belly to his office door.

00:01:16.929 --> 00:01:19.200
He reaches up and pulls down on the handle.

00:01:19.200 --> 00:01:21.829
There is a slight click as the latch releases.

00:01:21.829 --> 00:01:25.359
He opens the door just a crack and peers out
into the hallway.

00:01:25.359 --> 00:01:30.170
The flickering emergency lights illuminate
the corridor for a few seconds at a time before

00:01:30.170 --> 00:01:31.899
plunging it back into darkness.

00:01:31.899 --> 00:01:36.999
There is no one in sight, but from around
the corner flashes of light from machine gun

00:01:36.999 --> 00:01:38.729
fire flickers down the hall.

00:01:38.729 --> 00:01:42.709
The screams of the workers at Site-22 are
silenced.

00:01:42.709 --> 00:01:45.759
Pietro takes a deep breath and pushes the
door open further.

00:01:45.759 --> 00:01:49.929
He crawls out of his office and starts moving
away from the violence.

00:01:49.929 --> 00:01:55.799
Unfortunately, to get away from the mayhem
he must go deeper into the bowels of Site-22.

00:01:55.799 --> 00:02:00.299
The exit is the other way, but he is too scared
to head towards the armed men.

00:02:00.299 --> 00:02:03.889
He stands up and brushes the dirt from his
blue technician jumpsuit.

00:02:03.889 --> 00:02:06.840
The lights flicker off, the hallway goes dark.

00:02:06.840 --> 00:02:10.830
He reaches out his hands and comes into contact
with the cool damp wall.

00:02:10.830 --> 00:02:14.890
He feels his way down the corridor, swimming
in darkness.

00:02:14.890 --> 00:02:17.560
After a few moments the lights flicker back
on.

00:02:17.560 --> 00:02:21.450
Pietro looks over his shoulder to make sure
he is still in the clear.

00:02:21.450 --> 00:02:25.710
Standing at the end of the hall is a soldier
dressed in all black with a mask covering

00:02:25.710 --> 00:02:26.710
his face.

00:02:26.710 --> 00:02:28.420
The soldier stands motionless.

00:02:28.420 --> 00:02:34.170
Pietro turns to face the soldier, his eyes
open wide, his heart races, he can’t breath.

00:02:34.170 --> 00:02:35.190
The figure doesn’t move.

00:02:35.190 --> 00:02:40.200
Then the lights flicker out again and Pietro
pushes off the wall and runs, blind in the

00:02:40.200 --> 00:02:41.200
darkness.

00:02:41.200 --> 00:02:45.630
He sprints as fast as he can when suddenly
there is a loud crack and a bullet whizzes

00:02:45.630 --> 00:02:46.720
by his head.

00:02:46.720 --> 00:02:49.430
He can feel the wind as it barely misses his
cheek.

00:02:49.430 --> 00:02:50.760
He continues to run.

00:02:50.760 --> 00:02:53.820
The lights flicker back on, he peers over
his shoulder.

00:02:53.820 --> 00:02:58.580
Now there is an entire group of armed men
pursuing him down the hallway, guns raised.

00:02:58.580 --> 00:03:02.780
He turns the corner of the hallway and proceeds
down a set of stairs further into Site-22.

00:03:02.780 --> 00:03:07.810
At the bottom of the stairway there is a short
corridor with a door at the end of it.

00:03:07.810 --> 00:03:09.680
There’s nowhere else to go.

00:03:09.680 --> 00:03:12.120
He pulls a key card out of his pocket and
fumbles it.

00:03:12.120 --> 00:03:13.660
The card falls to the ground.

00:03:13.660 --> 00:03:18.180
Pietro bends down to pick it up and as he
leans over a bullet whizzes past where his

00:03:18.180 --> 00:03:19.540
head had just been.

00:03:19.540 --> 00:03:22.220
The projectile embeds itself into the metal
door.

00:03:22.220 --> 00:03:25.600
He scoops his key card up off the ground and
shoves it against the scanner.

00:03:25.600 --> 00:03:28.580
The door unlocks and he dashes into the room.

00:03:28.580 --> 00:03:30.680
He quickly turns and shuts the door.

00:03:30.680 --> 00:03:32.030
It locks automatically.

00:03:32.030 --> 00:03:35.790
The last thing he sees is the assassins running
towards the door.

00:03:35.790 --> 00:03:38.590
The lights flicker on in the room where Pietro
stands.

00:03:38.590 --> 00:03:42.710
The room has only one door, no windows, and
no vents.

00:03:42.710 --> 00:03:44.000
It is completely isolated.

00:03:44.000 --> 00:03:48.270
In the middle of the room is SCP-5000.

00:03:48.270 --> 00:03:52.230
He knew there was a SCP in this room that
was designated SCP-5000, but he never knew

00:03:52.230 --> 00:03:54.130
what it actually was.

00:03:54.130 --> 00:03:56.700
Here he is now, staring at it.

00:03:56.700 --> 00:04:00.670
A strange looking mechanical harness hanging
in the middle of the room.

00:04:00.670 --> 00:04:03.520
Suddenly, loud banging at the door fills the
room.

00:04:03.520 --> 00:04:05.260
The armed men are trying to break in.

00:04:05.260 --> 00:04:07.910
It is only a matter of time before they pry
the door open.

00:04:07.910 --> 00:04:11.490
With nowhere to go Pietro Wilson knows that
he is dead.

00:04:11.490 --> 00:04:14.180
He looks at SCP-5000 and shakes his head.

00:04:14.180 --> 00:04:16.690
“What do I have to lose?” he says out
loud.

00:04:16.690 --> 00:04:19.469
Only your life, a voice inside his head responds.

00:04:19.469 --> 00:04:23.330
He walks over to SCP-5000 and pulls it down
from where it's hanging.

00:04:23.330 --> 00:04:24.430
It is heavy.

00:04:24.430 --> 00:04:27.659
On the mechanical suit are symbols he does
not recognize.

00:04:27.659 --> 00:04:31.599
The only things he knows about the suit are
rumors he’s heard from others who work at

00:04:31.599 --> 00:04:32.599
Site-22.

00:04:32.599 --> 00:04:37.419
Supposedly, it first appeared in a flash of
light in the containment chamber of a Keter

00:04:37.419 --> 00:04:39.870
level SCP at Site-62C.

00:04:39.870 --> 00:04:43.490
The designation of this Keter was SCP-579.

00:04:43.490 --> 00:04:48.300
The only other thing that Pietro knows is
that everyone at Site-62C was slaughtered

00:04:48.300 --> 00:04:50.539
when containment was breached.

00:04:50.539 --> 00:04:54.650
SCP-5000 was found deactivated next to a pile
of bodies.

00:04:54.650 --> 00:05:00.710
He slips on the harness and Ss if it has a
life of its own, SCP-5000 begins to adjust

00:05:00.710 --> 00:05:03.639
itself to the exact dimensions of his body.

00:05:03.639 --> 00:05:08.479
The suit grows and snakes across his skin,
wrapping every appendage in armor.

00:05:08.479 --> 00:05:09.930
Then it begins to tighten.

00:05:09.930 --> 00:05:13.169
Pietro Wilson starts to scream as SCP-5000
envelops him.

00:05:13.169 --> 00:05:20.319
The suit rises up the back of his neck and
encases his entire head, silencing his screams.

00:05:20.319 --> 00:05:23.449
The door to the room blasts open from a controlled
explosion.

00:05:23.449 --> 00:05:26.699
As the dust and smoke settles the masked men
enter the room.

00:05:26.699 --> 00:05:30.599
Their flashlights move from side to side as
they search for the elusive technician who

00:05:30.599 --> 00:05:31.759
had just entered.

00:05:31.759 --> 00:05:32.759
There is no one in the room.

00:05:32.759 --> 00:05:36.529
All that is there is an empty rack in the
middle of the chamber.

00:05:36.529 --> 00:05:38.840
The men fan out, but there is no other exit.

00:05:38.840 --> 00:05:40.819
The room is just a solid square of concrete.

00:05:40.819 --> 00:05:41.819
They are baffled.

00:05:41.819 --> 00:05:43.979
“Where did he go?” one of them shouts.

00:05:43.979 --> 00:05:48.080
Pietro Wilson had blacked out from the pain
of the suit attaching to his body.

00:05:48.080 --> 00:05:51.120
He comes to still standing in the middle of
the room.

00:05:51.120 --> 00:05:53.219
All around him are men in black combat gear.

00:05:53.219 --> 00:05:54.840
They are searching for him.

00:05:54.840 --> 00:05:57.090
He holds his breath and closes his eyes.

00:05:57.090 --> 00:05:58.839
But the gun shots never come.

00:05:58.839 --> 00:06:00.439
He opens one of his eyes and looks around.

00:06:00.439 --> 00:06:03.040
Why haven’t they killed me yet? he thinks.

00:06:03.040 --> 00:06:06.819
He slowly turns his head as men walk by him
with their guns raised.

00:06:06.819 --> 00:06:08.599
He hears someone say, “where did he go?”

00:06:08.599 --> 00:06:09.880
I’m right here, he thinks.

00:06:09.880 --> 00:06:11.330
Am I dead?

00:06:11.330 --> 00:06:16.249
Pietro looks down to see that his entire body
is contained within SCP-5000.

00:06:16.249 --> 00:06:18.699
He lifts his hand and waves it in front of
his face.

00:06:18.699 --> 00:06:23.240
He is still clearly alive, but it seems as
if the killers can’t see him.

00:06:23.240 --> 00:06:27.499
He walks up to one of the mercenaries and
waves his hand in front of the man’s face.

00:06:27.499 --> 00:06:28.770
There is no reaction.

00:06:28.770 --> 00:06:31.279
The suit made me invisible, he thinks.

00:06:31.279 --> 00:06:35.159
Pietro looks at one of the men to see if he
can find out who they are and why they have

00:06:35.159 --> 00:06:36.830
killed everyone at the base.

00:06:36.830 --> 00:06:39.440
On the sleeve of the man’s jacket are the
words Zeta-19.

00:06:39.440 --> 00:06:44.270
He’s never heard of Zeta-19 before, but
they must be a part of an organization that

00:06:44.270 --> 00:06:46.970
is trying to undermine the SCP Foundation.

00:06:46.970 --> 00:06:51.180
The men continue to search the empty room,
clearly confused as to where the technician

00:06:51.180 --> 00:06:52.180
went.

00:06:52.180 --> 00:06:55.669
Pietro weaves his way through the group of
men and back out the door he had entered from.

00:06:55.669 --> 00:06:59.539
On his way through the wreckage that used
to be a door, Pietro Wilson trips on some

00:06:59.539 --> 00:07:00.539
debris.

00:07:00.539 --> 00:07:02.720
He reaches out to steady himself, but he is
falling.

00:07:02.720 --> 00:07:06.659
He closes his eyes knowing that as soon as
he hits the ground all of the men hunting

00:07:06.659 --> 00:07:09.080
him will be alerted by the sound of his fall.

00:07:09.080 --> 00:07:11.479
But the impact never comes.

00:07:11.479 --> 00:07:15.900
When Pietro opens his eyes it is as if he
is hovering just above the ground.

00:07:15.900 --> 00:07:17.400
He looks down at his feet.

00:07:17.400 --> 00:07:22.599
The toes of the suit are firmly planted on
the floor like powerful magnets on iron.

00:07:22.599 --> 00:07:28.189
SCP-5000 has prevented his fall and is holding
him in place using the feet of the suit only.

00:07:28.189 --> 00:07:30.809
He reaches out his hand and gently places
it on the ground.

00:07:30.809 --> 00:07:33.779
He pushes himself up to a standing position.

00:07:33.779 --> 00:07:37.999
He turns to look back into the room, the men
are still in there searching for him.

00:07:37.999 --> 00:07:40.689
Pietro makes his way back through Site-22.

00:07:40.689 --> 00:07:44.349
He walks by his office and proceeds towards
the exit of the facility.

00:07:44.349 --> 00:07:49.660
As he passes the labs and other rooms at Site-22
all he finds is carnage.

00:07:49.660 --> 00:07:50.899
Everyone has been killed.

00:07:50.899 --> 00:07:54.909
An extra bullet has been placed in each person’s
head to make sure.

00:07:54.909 --> 00:08:00.479
It seems that the only mission these men were
on was to kill everyone, and make sure they

00:08:00.479 --> 00:08:01.710
stayed dead.

00:08:01.710 --> 00:08:05.719
He continues towards the exit of Site-22 that
is guarded by two men.

00:08:05.719 --> 00:08:10.419
As he approaches the two heavily armed men,
Pietro makes sure to be as quiet as possible.

00:08:10.419 --> 00:08:15.819
This is not a difficult task as the SCP-5000
has given him stealth capabilities.

00:08:15.819 --> 00:08:19.319
He notices that even his footsteps aren’t
giving off any sound.

00:08:19.319 --> 00:08:23.110
It is almost as if the suit is allowing him
to glide across the floor.

00:08:23.110 --> 00:08:27.123
He is almost to the exit, then he will be
home free.

00:08:27.123 --> 00:08:32.370
He takes a deep breath, turns sideways, and
squeezes past the two men guarding the doorway.

00:08:32.370 --> 00:08:37.710
Just as he is about to leave this nightmare
behind, one of the guards turns unexpectedly.

00:08:37.710 --> 00:08:41.380
The man’s shoulder runs directly into Pietro
Wilson throwing him off balance.

00:08:41.380 --> 00:08:44.980
He is knocked into the second guard, both
of the men begin to scream.

00:08:44.980 --> 00:08:46.500
“What is that?” one of them shouts.

00:08:46.500 --> 00:08:50.510
They begin to raise their guns on the invisible
object that just bumped into them.

00:08:50.510 --> 00:08:55.270
It’s then that SCP-5000 takes over Pietro’s
body.

00:08:55.270 --> 00:08:58.450
The suit raises his arm and grabs one of the
men by the throat.

00:08:58.450 --> 00:09:00.830
With a squeeze the man’s larynx is instantly
crushed.

00:09:00.830 --> 00:09:03.740
Then the suit twists slightly and snaps the
man’s neck.

00:09:03.740 --> 00:09:05.770
It turns to face the second man.

00:09:05.770 --> 00:09:10.130
Even the black mask the man is weaning can’t
hide the look of terror on his face, but Pietro

00:09:10.130 --> 00:09:12.840
has no control over what SCP-5000 is doing.

00:09:12.840 --> 00:09:14.790
He has never killed before.

00:09:14.790 --> 00:09:18.980
The suit launches Pietro’s body into the
second man, pinning him against the wall.

00:09:18.980 --> 00:09:24.080
It then grabs the top of the mercenary’s
head and slams it against the concrete again,

00:09:24.080 --> 00:09:29.210
and again, and again, until the man’s screams
are silenced.

00:09:29.210 --> 00:09:33.880
The suit lets go of the man and his lifeless
body slides to the ground as Pietro blacks

00:09:33.880 --> 00:09:34.880
out.

00:09:34.880 --> 00:09:39.320
When he regains consciousness, he’s outside
of Site-22 standing on top of a hill, looking

00:09:39.320 --> 00:09:41.170
down at the facility below.

00:09:41.170 --> 00:09:43.550
He looks at his hands, then at the rest of
his body.

00:09:43.550 --> 00:09:47.080
He is still contained within SCP-5000.

00:09:47.080 --> 00:09:49.850
There is a flash of light and a heads up display
comes on.

00:09:49.850 --> 00:09:54.050
He doesn’t recognize any of the symbols,
but as his eyes move from one area of the

00:09:54.050 --> 00:09:57.290
screen to the next, the symbols become highlighted.

00:09:57.290 --> 00:10:00.880
Before his eyes certain symbols begin to translate
into words he can read.

00:10:00.880 --> 00:10:03.900
One of the symbols now says: Journal Entry.

00:10:03.900 --> 00:10:07.650
Unsure of what else to do, Pietro begins recounting
what happened to him at Site-22.

00:10:07.650 --> 00:10:12.480
He makes his way through the desert towards
the nearest SCP Foundation safe house.

00:10:12.480 --> 00:10:16.860
He knows once there he will be able to reach
out to his superiors for help and further

00:10:16.860 --> 00:10:17.860
orders.

00:10:17.860 --> 00:10:21.350
Maybe he can even find a way to get SCP-5000
to release him.

00:10:21.350 --> 00:10:25.980
As he trudges along, Pietro Wilson notices
that his brain is telling him he is thirsty.

00:10:25.980 --> 00:10:29.290
But the vitals on the suit’s heads up display
say he is in good health.

00:10:29.290 --> 00:10:32.950
In fact, he is better than good, his vitals
are all perfect.

00:10:32.950 --> 00:10:36.370
The suit seems to be giving him all the nutrients
his body needs.

00:10:36.370 --> 00:10:39.810
It has even fixed his busted knee that was
injured back in college playing football.

00:10:39.810 --> 00:10:42.600
The joint itself has somehow been healed.

00:10:42.600 --> 00:10:45.870
Pietro finally reaches the safe house and
opens the door.

00:10:45.870 --> 00:10:47.340
It is quiet and dusty.

00:10:47.340 --> 00:10:49.700
It looks as if no one has been there in years.

00:10:49.700 --> 00:10:54.150
He walks over to the communications station
and tries to contact the Foundation but all

00:10:54.150 --> 00:10:55.370
he gets is static.

00:10:55.370 --> 00:10:57.660
He gives up and walks over to the TV.

00:10:57.660 --> 00:11:00.740
He pushes the on button, the screen hisses
to life.

00:11:00.740 --> 00:11:03.410
What he sees causes his jaw to drop.

00:11:03.410 --> 00:11:08.870
SCPs had been let loose around the world and
were killing people by the millions.

00:11:08.870 --> 00:11:10.230
What was going on?

00:11:10.230 --> 00:11:12.140
Pietro was startled awake from a nightmare.

00:11:12.140 --> 00:11:17.470
He was hyperventilating, but his body almost
immediately recovered, and his breathing slowed.

00:11:17.470 --> 00:11:20.140
A heads up display flashed on infront of his
eyes.

00:11:20.140 --> 00:11:23.010
Pietro Wilson was still contained within SCP-5000.

00:11:23.010 --> 00:11:26.870
The suit would not let him go.

00:11:26.870 --> 00:11:31.580
He instinctively went to rub his eyes, but
the metal hands of the suit just clanked against

00:11:31.580 --> 00:11:33.890
the helmet that covered his head.

00:11:33.890 --> 00:11:36.630
He wanted out of this suit!

00:11:36.630 --> 00:11:39.370
Pietro stood up and walked over to the television.

00:11:39.370 --> 00:11:41.850
He reached out to turn it on but paused.

00:11:41.850 --> 00:11:46.310
He thought: Do I really want to see how bad
things have gotten since I fell asleep?

00:11:46.310 --> 00:11:48.480
But he had to know.

00:11:48.480 --> 00:11:52.450
He was filled with dread as the TV came on
and he saw the first images.

00:11:52.450 --> 00:11:57.680
The world looked as if it was ending, and
it seemed like the SCP Foundation was responsible.

00:11:57.680 --> 00:12:00.100
How could this be?

00:12:00.100 --> 00:12:03.700
They were supposed to protect humanity not
destroy it.

00:12:03.700 --> 00:12:07.200
Pietro needed to uncover the truth behind
what was happening.

00:12:07.200 --> 00:12:12.960
SCP-5000 had a log entry function that he
could use to record everything he uncovered.

00:12:12.960 --> 00:12:17.650
Even if he didn’t make it out of this alive,
maybe one day someone would find the suit

00:12:17.650 --> 00:12:20.060
and be able to access what he had learned.

00:12:20.060 --> 00:12:24.220
The date of his first journal entry was February
1, 2020.

00:12:24.220 --> 00:12:28.940
As Pietro watched the carnage unfold on TV,
he began to put together the pieces of what

00:12:28.940 --> 00:12:30.710
he had witnessed himself.

00:12:30.710 --> 00:12:35.480
He knew a special-ops squad had executed everyone
at Site-22 where he worked.

00:12:35.480 --> 00:12:38.060
He knew that the SCPs had been let loose.

00:12:38.060 --> 00:12:41.760
He knew the world was ending… but why?

00:12:41.760 --> 00:12:44.450
As Pietro pondered this, a newscaster appeared.

00:12:44.450 --> 00:12:48.620
“What you have just witnessed are reports
from around the world of monsters ravaging

00:12:48.620 --> 00:12:50.450
cities and towns.

00:12:50.450 --> 00:12:54.960
This all started with a mysterious message
from an organization that calls itself the

00:12:54.960 --> 00:12:56.100
SCP Foundation.

00:12:56.100 --> 00:13:00.670
Their ruling body, named the O5 Council, released
the following statement: ‘For those who

00:13:00.670 --> 00:13:05.311
are not currently aware of our existence,
we represent the organization known as the

00:13:05.311 --> 00:13:07.230
SCP Foundation.

00:13:07.230 --> 00:13:11.650
Our previous mission centered around the containment
and study of anomalous objects, entities,

00:13:11.650 --> 00:13:13.790
and other assorted phenomena.

00:13:13.790 --> 00:13:18.770
This mission was the focus of our organization
for more than one-hundred years.

00:13:18.770 --> 00:13:23.690
Due to circumstances outside of our control,
this directive has now changed.

00:13:23.690 --> 00:13:27.430
Our new mission will be the extermination
of the human race.

00:13:27.430 --> 00:13:30.430
There will be no further communication.”

00:13:30.430 --> 00:13:32.500
He couldn’t believe what he was seeing.

00:13:32.500 --> 00:13:35.380
The SCP Foundation had declared war on the
human race.

00:13:35.380 --> 00:13:36.950
How could this be?

00:13:36.950 --> 00:13:42.140
What had led to the O5 council changing their
entire mission from protecting humanity to

00:13:42.140 --> 00:13:43.140
ending it?

00:13:43.140 --> 00:13:48.160
Could it be possible that a powerful SCP had
taken control or influenced the council’s

00:13:48.160 --> 00:13:49.160
decision?

00:13:49.160 --> 00:13:52.970
Pietro turned on the radio, flipped through
TV channels, and scoured the internet for

00:13:52.970 --> 00:13:56.730
information on what had happened over the
past 24 hours.

00:13:56.730 --> 00:14:01.530
The first image he saw was a human-like creature
with arms and legs twice as long as they should

00:14:01.530 --> 00:14:06.870
have been, with deep black eyes, and a mouth
curled up into a silent scream showing teeth

00:14:06.870 --> 00:14:09.210
as sharp as razor blades.

00:14:09.210 --> 00:14:14.910
From the files he could access Pietro learned
that this was SCP-096, a creature that was

00:14:14.910 --> 00:14:20.600
docile until someone saw its face, at which
point the SCP would start to shriek and cry,

00:14:20.600 --> 00:14:24.280
before hunting down whoever saw its face and
slaughtering them.

00:14:24.280 --> 00:14:26.000
He quickly changed the channel.

00:14:26.000 --> 00:14:30.770
The file said that even if SCP-096 was seen
on a screen, it would find the viewer and

00:14:30.770 --> 00:14:32.670
tear them limb from limb.

00:14:32.670 --> 00:14:34.170
Surely that couldn’t be true.

00:14:34.170 --> 00:14:37.580
There were potentially millions of people
who had just seen it on TV.

00:14:37.580 --> 00:14:39.790
What would happen to them?

00:14:39.790 --> 00:14:41.890
What would happen to him?

00:14:41.890 --> 00:14:45.720
On the next channel was footage of a gigantic
animal in the middle of the ocean.

00:14:45.720 --> 00:14:50.690
This was SCP-169, a leviathan from the Pre-Cambrian
era.

00:14:50.690 --> 00:14:55.810
The creature was around 5,000 kilometers long
and slowly swam just below the surface of

00:14:55.810 --> 00:14:56.810
the ocean.

00:14:56.810 --> 00:15:01.580
The feed suddenly changed to footage of devastating
tsunamis and destruction caused by earthquakes.

00:15:01.580 --> 00:15:06.920
When SCP-169 had been awoken from its slumber
by the Foundation detonating nukes on its

00:15:06.920 --> 00:15:09.640
back, it began trying to escape the danger.

00:15:09.640 --> 00:15:14.800
The movement of the massive creature caused
natural disasters, destroying coastal communities

00:15:14.800 --> 00:15:16.630
around the world.

00:15:16.630 --> 00:15:21.130
On another channel Pietro watched as the chancellor
of Germany gave a speech, announcing that

00:15:21.130 --> 00:15:24.760
the country was declaring war on the SCP Foundation.

00:15:24.760 --> 00:15:27.230
Off camera the sound of a tinkling bell could
be heard.

00:15:27.230 --> 00:15:31.830
A man dressed as a Victorian era butler entered
and picked up a pen from the Chancellor's

00:15:31.830 --> 00:15:33.540
desk.

00:15:33.540 --> 00:15:37.320
He approached the Chancellor and raised the
pen in the air as the camera cut away, but

00:15:37.320 --> 00:15:41.430
the sound of gunshots and yelling could be
heard before the feed went dead.

00:15:41.430 --> 00:15:45.850
The news reported that similar events involving
world leaders by the exact same butler had

00:15:45.850 --> 00:15:49.430
been occurring since the SCP Foundation changed
its mission.

00:15:49.430 --> 00:15:52.900
Pietro searched through the suit’s files
to try and figure out what was happening and

00:15:52.900 --> 00:15:57.060
found that SCP-662 must have been connected.

00:15:57.060 --> 00:16:02.380
Next was a strange skin disease plaguing New
York and Delhi designated SCP-610 that covered

00:16:02.380 --> 00:16:07.250
its host in rashes and boils before seeking
to take over their bodies.

00:16:07.250 --> 00:16:11.070
Finally some good news though, as the outbreak
looked to be contained by the combined efforts

00:16:11.070 --> 00:16:15.510
of the Global Occult Coalition and the Church
of the Broken God.

00:16:15.510 --> 00:16:20.310
And then some bad news, as SCP-682 had also
been released.

00:16:20.310 --> 00:16:24.920
A massive crocodilian monster, it’s sole
mission was to destroy all life.

00:16:24.920 --> 00:16:30.600
It was fueled by hatred for living things,
making it the perfect tool of the O5 Council’s

00:16:30.600 --> 00:16:32.070
new stated mission.

00:16:32.070 --> 00:16:37.290
Pietro had heard rumors of SCPs that could
instantly end the world, but clearly the Foundation

00:16:37.290 --> 00:16:40.370
hadn’t gone down this route… yet.

00:16:40.370 --> 00:16:44.290
Did they want to keep the rest of the planet
intact, or maybe there were hold outs in the

00:16:44.290 --> 00:16:49.800
SCP Foundation who were trying to stop the
O5 Council from carrying out their mission?

00:16:49.800 --> 00:16:55.630
All Pietro knew was that right now, there
were some real nasty SCPs running around wreaking

00:16:55.630 --> 00:16:56.630
havoc.

00:16:56.630 --> 00:16:59.330
Pietro suddenly heard an explosion in the
distance.

00:16:59.330 --> 00:17:02.590
Far away, but still close enough to make him
nervous.

00:17:02.590 --> 00:17:06.010
Maybe he was better off staying in the safehouse
and waiting out the apocalypse.

00:17:06.010 --> 00:17:10.710
The suit was keeping him healthy, nourished,
and undetectable to foes.

00:17:10.710 --> 00:17:14.660
Any sane person would have remained there
in seclusion and safety, but Pietro needed

00:17:14.660 --> 00:17:15.850
answers.

00:17:15.850 --> 00:17:20.540
He felt it was his responsibility to log and
try to make sense of everything the SCP Foundation

00:17:20.540 --> 00:17:21.540
was doing.

00:17:21.540 --> 00:17:25.260
He brought up a map of SCP sites in the area
on his display.

00:17:25.260 --> 00:17:26.439
The closest was Site-19.

00:17:26.439 --> 00:17:31.610
It was time to venture out into the end of
the world and find some answers.

00:17:31.610 --> 00:17:34.730
But he was about to be faced with even more
questions.

00:17:34.730 --> 00:17:40.310
On the way to Site-19, Pietro came across
something strange - a squad of Foundation

00:17:40.310 --> 00:17:41.570
soldiers in a clearing.

00:17:41.570 --> 00:17:46.690
They were standing at attention as their commander
paced back and forth, up and down the line.

00:17:46.690 --> 00:17:51.410
The soldiers' uniforms had the insignia “MTF
Epsilon-6” embroidered on them.

00:17:51.410 --> 00:17:55.110
The commander stopped in front of the first
soldier in the line, clapped her hands, and

00:17:55.110 --> 00:17:58.260
informed the soldier she would be beginning
the check now.

00:17:58.260 --> 00:18:02.300
The commander pulled out a long knife and
plunged it into the soldier’s shoulder.

00:18:02.300 --> 00:18:07.220
Strangely, the soldier did not move, make
a sound, or react in any way.

00:18:07.220 --> 00:18:10.930
She moved to the next soldier and repeated
the same process.

00:18:10.930 --> 00:18:14.240
This continued down the line until she reached
the eighth soldier.

00:18:14.240 --> 00:18:19.290
This time when the commander stabbed the shoulder
of the soldier, he noticeably winced and cried

00:18:19.290 --> 00:18:20.330
out in pain.

00:18:20.330 --> 00:18:22.820
The commander shouted “got a live one!”

00:18:22.820 --> 00:18:26.710
Pietro watched as the soldiers raised their
guns and fired at the one who had cried out.

00:18:26.710 --> 00:18:28.850
He dropped to the ground.

00:18:28.850 --> 00:18:32.440
The commander moved on to the last soldier
and put the knife in his shoulder.

00:18:32.440 --> 00:18:33.440
There was no reaction.

00:18:33.440 --> 00:18:36.020
“Alright we’re clear,” yelled the commander.

00:18:36.020 --> 00:18:37.960
“Let’s move out!”

00:18:37.960 --> 00:18:42.640
Pietro waited until the squad was out of sight
and made his way to the corpse lying on the

00:18:42.640 --> 00:18:43.640
ground.

00:18:43.640 --> 00:18:47.600
He scavenged weapons and basic medical supplies,
then he buried the body and recorded what

00:18:47.600 --> 00:18:50.600
he had seen in SCP-5000’s log.

00:18:50.600 --> 00:18:54.570
He had no idea why this soldier was killed,
or why the others didn’t feel pain.

00:18:54.570 --> 00:18:57.240
Maybe they weren’t human at all?

00:18:57.240 --> 00:19:00.630
Maybe it was a squad of SCPs that had a human
infiltrate their ranks?

00:19:00.630 --> 00:19:06.290
None of this makes sense, Piertro thought,
before continuing on.

00:19:06.290 --> 00:19:11.720
Upon reaching Site-19, Pietro found it in
disarray, and worse, practically all of the

00:19:11.720 --> 00:19:14.730
SCPs that were held at the site had breached
containment.

00:19:14.730 --> 00:19:20.470
He was able to walk into the compound unnoticed
and deep in the facility he found scientists

00:19:20.470 --> 00:19:24.460
and researchers going about their business
as if they had no idea what was happening

00:19:24.460 --> 00:19:25.921
out in the world.

00:19:25.921 --> 00:19:28.790
They must have been following the orders of
the O5 Council.

00:19:28.790 --> 00:19:32.850
Pietro listened in on conversations about
how to create the maximum number of human

00:19:32.850 --> 00:19:36.580
casualties, and which SCP should be released
next.

00:19:36.580 --> 00:19:40.140
He felt a deep hatred for the people in this
facility.

00:19:40.140 --> 00:19:44.230
How could they be so casual about wiping out
humanity?

00:19:44.230 --> 00:19:48.560
As he observed more of the workers at Site-19,
he noticed something strange.

00:19:48.560 --> 00:19:53.520
Everyones’ eyes were cold and dead, like
there was no humanity left in them, as if

00:19:53.520 --> 00:19:57.880
something had gotten to these scientists and
removed the very souls from their bodies.

00:19:57.880 --> 00:20:02.120
Pietro stealthily stole a senior staff member’s
credentials and found an empty office where

00:20:02.120 --> 00:20:06.390
he could access logs from the facility, to
try and get a better idea of the timeline

00:20:06.390 --> 00:20:10.560
of events that led to the SCP Foundation’s
war on humanity.

00:20:10.560 --> 00:20:14.840
He logged into the mainframe and brought up
entries from the end of the previous year.

00:20:14.840 --> 00:20:19.790
He found that late in 2019 a project called
‘PNEUMA’ became of great interest to the

00:20:19.790 --> 00:20:21.220
O5 council.

00:20:21.220 --> 00:20:24.809
From what Pietro could tell, the project had
something to do with the collective human

00:20:24.809 --> 00:20:27.790
consciousness, also called the psychospace.

00:20:27.790 --> 00:20:32.900
Apparently, SCP researchers had a breakthrough
in mapping out the psychospace.

00:20:32.900 --> 00:20:37.030
Unfortunately, many of the files had been
redacted, and there was no way for Pietro

00:20:37.030 --> 00:20:39.600
to access the unredacted version.

00:20:39.600 --> 00:20:43.390
After ‘PNEUMA’ had been brought to the
attention of the O5 Council, a series of orders

00:20:43.390 --> 00:20:48.880
were sent to all senior staff and site directors
but frustratingly these orders had also been

00:20:48.880 --> 00:20:49.880
redacted.

00:20:49.880 --> 00:20:54.010
All he could see was that after the orders
were sent out, a wave of resignations were

00:20:54.010 --> 00:20:56.110
submitted across the Foundation.

00:20:56.110 --> 00:21:01.650
Suspiciously, a wave of suicides had also
occurred at roughly the same time.

00:21:01.650 --> 00:21:03.240
What was in these orders?!

00:21:03.240 --> 00:21:07.580
The 05 council then sent out a number of files
to all senior staff and site directors with

00:21:07.580 --> 00:21:12.300
instructions to disseminate the materials
among those serving under them, after which

00:21:12.300 --> 00:21:15.890
both the resignations and deaths immediately
ceased.

00:21:15.890 --> 00:21:21.480
Pietro searched everywhere for what was in
those files, but like so much of the SCP database,

00:21:21.480 --> 00:21:24.210
this information had been redacted as well.

00:21:24.210 --> 00:21:28.590
What was clear was that the SCP Foundation
had begun gearing up for the extermination

00:21:28.590 --> 00:21:31.130
of humanity the following year.

00:21:31.130 --> 00:21:37.400
The entry log for February 1, 2020 read: “Mobile
Task Forces are dispatched to all Exclusionary

00:21:37.400 --> 00:21:39.440
Sites to execute all personnel.

00:21:39.440 --> 00:21:44.920
Immediately following the conclusion of these
missions, the Foundation declares war on humanity.”

00:21:44.920 --> 00:21:47.780
This was where Pietro Wilson’s journey had
started.

00:21:47.780 --> 00:21:51.290
He slammed his hands down on the computer
monitor in frustration.

00:21:51.290 --> 00:21:55.580
The suit absorbed all of the impact and crushed
the monitor in half.

00:21:55.580 --> 00:21:59.380
Pietro moved to a new, non smashed computer,
and logged in again.

00:21:59.380 --> 00:22:04.070
This time he brought up the most current entries
to see what the O5 Council was up to recently

00:22:04.070 --> 00:22:06.130
to see if there were some answers in the present.

00:22:06.130 --> 00:22:10.240
The SCP Foundation had been busy while he
was making his way to Site-19.

00:22:10.240 --> 00:22:16.360
They had released SCP-1048 in Paris, which
now led a horde of bears down the Champs Elysées.

00:22:16.360 --> 00:22:20.430
In the distance Pietro thought he could almost
make out a massive red teddy bear walking

00:22:20.430 --> 00:22:22.100
between the buildings.

00:22:22.100 --> 00:22:27.610
The SCP Foundation was also launching counterattacks
on any organization that tried to oppose them.

00:22:27.610 --> 00:22:31.730
They used SCP-1290 to hurl projectiles at
the Global Occult Coalition’s base.

00:22:31.730 --> 00:22:36.710
They were also using SCP-1440 to brainwash
people and convince them that they needed

00:22:36.710 --> 00:22:37.710
to riot.

00:22:37.710 --> 00:22:42.070
This caused widespread destruction as people
panicked and were trampled to death.

00:22:42.070 --> 00:22:46.890
Pietro thought it was sad that such a kind
looking old man could cause so much destruction.

00:22:46.890 --> 00:22:51.580
He recorded as much as he could before deciding
that it was time to get out of Site-19.

00:22:51.580 --> 00:22:57.140
Although SCP-5000 still made him undetectable,
he couldn’t shake the feeling that the lifeless

00:22:57.140 --> 00:23:02.010
eyes of the staff were beginning to look his
way more and more often.

00:23:02.010 --> 00:23:07.650
As Pietro exited Site-19, the sky glowed orange
with the fire of countless burning buildings.

00:23:07.650 --> 00:23:10.610
He needed to find more answers.

00:23:10.610 --> 00:23:14.920
He needed to uncover the reason the SCP Foundation
was trying to wipe out humanity.

00:23:14.920 --> 00:23:19.180
He had learned a lot from Site-19, and was
sure that if he could just get to the next

00:23:19.180 --> 00:23:23.440
site, he would finally be able to figure out
the Foundation’s motive, and maybe even

00:23:23.440 --> 00:23:24.880
how to stop them.

00:23:24.880 --> 00:23:29.250
He took a step forward but his heads up display
suddenly went completely dark.

00:23:29.250 --> 00:23:33.630
The suit constricted tighter around his body,
slowing the blood flow to his brain.

00:23:33.630 --> 00:23:40.500
He couldn’t move as his vision got dimmer,
and dimmer, and dimmer, until he blacked out.

00:23:40.500 --> 00:23:42.070
“What happened?”

00:23:42.070 --> 00:23:47.520
Pietro says out loud as he looks at his vitals
in the heads up display of SCP-5000.

00:23:47.520 --> 00:23:51.580
He is still contained within the exclusionary
suit that makes him undetectable to human

00:23:51.580 --> 00:23:52.700
senses.

00:23:52.700 --> 00:23:54.800
He checks the date and gasps in surprise.

00:23:54.800 --> 00:23:55.860
“Three months!

00:23:55.860 --> 00:23:59.500
I’ve been passed out for three months!”

00:23:59.500 --> 00:24:02.460
He stands up and looks across the barren landscape.

00:24:02.460 --> 00:24:06.220
The screen inside the suit indicates he has
traversed half of the country since he left

00:24:06.220 --> 00:24:08.990
Site-19 three months ago.

00:24:08.990 --> 00:24:10.960
Pietro looks down at one of his hands.

00:24:10.960 --> 00:24:12.830
He is holding a black leather briefcase.

00:24:12.830 --> 00:24:14.980
“Where did that come from?” he wonders.

00:24:14.980 --> 00:24:20.980
Pietro has no idea what is inside the briefcase,
but he knows it definitely isn’t round.

00:24:20.980 --> 00:24:23.809
He tries to let it go, his fingers won’t
open.

00:24:23.809 --> 00:24:28.280
He uses his other hand to try and pry the
briefcase away from himself, but his hand

00:24:28.280 --> 00:24:29.960
only clasps to it harder.

00:24:29.960 --> 00:24:33.210
Then a wave of calm washes over him.

00:24:33.210 --> 00:24:38.530
Something inside his head speaks to him, but
it’s not a voice, more like a feeling.

00:24:38.530 --> 00:24:43.090
It is a sense of purpose, and Pietro’s new
mission in life is to deliver this briefcase

00:24:43.090 --> 00:24:48.270
to SCP-579, nothing else is as important.

00:24:48.270 --> 00:24:52.240
Pietro Wilson takes a deep breath and embraces
his new purpose in life.

00:24:52.240 --> 00:24:57.460
He still wants to uncover the reason that
the SCP Foundation is trying to wipe out humanity,

00:24:57.460 --> 00:25:03.040
but this will have to wait until he delivers
the briefcase to SCP-579.

00:25:03.040 --> 00:25:08.540
Pietro does not know exactly where 579 is
located, but he can feel a pull in a certain

00:25:08.540 --> 00:25:11.240
direction, so he begins to walk.

00:25:11.240 --> 00:25:16.380
Pietro brings up the information stored in
the SCP-5000 suit from the Foundation’s

00:25:16.380 --> 00:25:17.540
database.

00:25:17.540 --> 00:25:22.820
He finds that all information about what SCP-579
is has been expunged from the record.

00:25:22.820 --> 00:25:27.530
The only useful information in the file is
that the Keter level SCP is located at Site-62c.

00:25:27.530 --> 00:25:31.920
At least Pietro has a destination to aim for.

00:25:31.920 --> 00:25:34.780
He travels for days without seeing a living
soul.

00:25:34.780 --> 00:25:37.110
But he does pass thousands of corpses.

00:25:37.110 --> 00:25:43.380
He tries to ignore them but one stands out
to him inside a house as he searches for supplies.

00:25:43.380 --> 00:25:46.150
It's the body of a recently deceased boy.

00:25:46.150 --> 00:25:48.870
He couldn't have been more than eight years
old.

00:25:48.870 --> 00:25:51.790
He was so young, Pietro thinks.

00:25:51.790 --> 00:25:55.950
He bends over to scoop up the body and bury
it outside.

00:25:55.950 --> 00:25:59.720
As his hand touches the body, the boy’s
skin begins to move.

00:25:59.720 --> 00:26:04.160
It is as if hundreds of tiny creatures are
scurrying just under the skin.

00:26:04.160 --> 00:26:08.110
Then, from out of every orifice, comes hundreds
of little pale worms.

00:26:08.110 --> 00:26:11.000
each with the face of the boy.

00:26:11.000 --> 00:26:16.410
They are all cackling as they crawl off the
boy’s body and into a drain a few feet away.

00:26:16.410 --> 00:26:18.000
Pietro jumps back and runs.

00:26:18.000 --> 00:26:21.440
That is the last person I try to bury, he
thinks.

00:26:21.440 --> 00:26:26.790
Pietro pushes forward, the hundreds of little
laughing worms haunting his thoughts, until

00:26:26.790 --> 00:26:31.970
he puts a significant distance between himself
and the little boy’s body.

00:26:31.970 --> 00:26:35.580
Pietro continues to walk towards the direction
of Site-62c.

00:26:35.580 --> 00:26:39.750
He passes more corpses, but decides to stay
clear of them.

00:26:39.750 --> 00:26:44.110
Although the suit makes it so Pietro doesn’t
need to rest, he can only go so fast.

00:26:44.110 --> 00:26:49.100
He enters a small abandoned town that looks
like something out of an old western movie.

00:26:49.100 --> 00:26:51.910
A tumbleweed blows across the dirt road.

00:26:51.910 --> 00:26:55.870
Pietro sits on the wooden step of the local
saloon and takes a break.

00:26:55.870 --> 00:26:57.990
He looks down at the briefcase in his hand.

00:26:57.990 --> 00:27:03.260
He hasn’t had the urge to open it, only
to deliver it to SCP-579.

00:27:03.260 --> 00:27:05.310
Pietro puts the black briefcase on his lap.

00:27:05.310 --> 00:27:10.700
He stares at it and slides his hands along
the leather, stops with his thumb on the latch,

00:27:10.700 --> 00:27:11.700
and pushes.

00:27:11.700 --> 00:27:13.230
The silver locks snap open.

00:27:13.230 --> 00:27:19.670
Pietro opens the briefcase... a bright light
beams out, and he passes out.

00:27:19.670 --> 00:27:24.190
When Pietro comes to again he is miles closer
to Site-62c.

00:27:24.190 --> 00:27:26.820
There is a warm feeling enveloping his body.

00:27:26.820 --> 00:27:29.950
He looks down at the briefcase which is now
closed.

00:27:29.950 --> 00:27:35.220
Wow, this thing is like my own personal skip
button, Pietro thinks.

00:27:35.220 --> 00:27:41.090
He holds up the briefcase, unlatches the locks,
sees the bright light, and passes out again.

00:27:41.090 --> 00:27:44.770
He awakes once again miles away from his last
position.

00:27:44.770 --> 00:27:46.840
So it wasn’t just a one-off effect.

00:27:46.840 --> 00:27:51.950
Pietro continues walking across the country,
switching between using his own legs and whatever

00:27:51.950 --> 00:27:54.480
magic is contained within the briefcase.

00:27:54.480 --> 00:27:57.490
He is making faster progress now.

00:27:57.490 --> 00:28:01.870
As he walks through a dense deciduous forest
he comes across a pack of wolves eating the

00:28:01.870 --> 00:28:04.040
remains of an SCP Agent.

00:28:04.040 --> 00:28:09.309
Pietro is undetectable to the wolves thanks
to the SCP-5000 suit and he makes his way

00:28:09.309 --> 00:28:13.890
over to the pack, quietly grabbing a laptop
laying on the ground next to the agent’s

00:28:13.890 --> 00:28:14.890
body.

00:28:14.890 --> 00:28:19.100
Pietro takes the laptop and goes a way deeper
into the forest before stopping to boot up

00:28:19.100 --> 00:28:20.100
the computer.

00:28:20.100 --> 00:28:24.620
He has not forgotten about the horrors the
SCP Foundation has released and he needs to

00:28:24.620 --> 00:28:28.429
know how the world has been doing over the
last few months.

00:28:28.429 --> 00:28:30.740
What he finds is... not good.

00:28:30.740 --> 00:28:37.460
The SCP Foundation has triggered the eruption
of Yellowstone destroying SCP-2000, which

00:28:37.460 --> 00:28:42.110
unknown to Pietro, contained the failsafe
for rebuilding human society in the event

00:28:42.110 --> 00:28:47.490
of a world ending scenario, which this was
starting to look more and more like.

00:28:47.490 --> 00:28:51.680
It was only a matter of time now before the
soot and ash thrown up by the eruption blocks

00:28:51.680 --> 00:28:55.730
out the sun in much of what is left of the
United States.

00:28:55.730 --> 00:29:01.429
The Foundation has also found a way to get
SCP-2241 to do their dirty work at refugee

00:29:01.429 --> 00:29:02.429
camps.

00:29:02.429 --> 00:29:06.290
The young brown haired boy is most likely
being manipulated by the Foundation under

00:29:06.290 --> 00:29:09.940
the pretenses that they are only doing what’s
best for “their” child.

00:29:09.940 --> 00:29:14.880
He has caused whole groups of refugees to
turn on eachother, leading to a massacre.

00:29:14.880 --> 00:29:19.330
The last entry says that the young boy is
being sent to the The Global Occult Coalition

00:29:19.330 --> 00:29:24.770
hold out at Ganzir, to help destroy some of
the last threats to the SCP Foundation.

00:29:24.770 --> 00:29:29.170
A series of other SCPs have been dispatched
by the Foundation around the world to continue

00:29:29.170 --> 00:29:30.880
the destruction of humanity.

00:29:30.880 --> 00:29:35.900
They even managed to use temporal anomalies
to make it Christmas time everywhere around

00:29:35.900 --> 00:29:42.870
the world so SCP-4666, the brutal Yule-tide
creature that stalks the homes of children,

00:29:42.870 --> 00:29:45.950
is free to cause chaos.

00:29:45.950 --> 00:29:47.950
Pietro had seen enough.

00:29:47.950 --> 00:29:53.210
He slams the laptop shut, throws it against
the trunk of a tree., and opens the briefcase

00:29:53.210 --> 00:29:54.210
again.

00:29:54.210 --> 00:29:58.160
He awakes standing feet away from a group
of Global Occult Coalition soldiers who are

00:29:58.160 --> 00:30:00.020
sitting around a campfire.

00:30:00.020 --> 00:30:04.320
Maybe they know why the SCP Foundation is
trying to end the world, he thinks.

00:30:04.320 --> 00:30:08.650
He decides that it is too risky to show himself
to the soldiers, but takes some solace in

00:30:08.650 --> 00:30:12.630
sitting around the campfire with other living
humans.

00:30:12.630 --> 00:30:16.390
The soldiers are sharing stories about what
is happening, one catches the attention of

00:30:16.390 --> 00:30:17.760
Pietro Wilson.

00:30:17.760 --> 00:30:23.559
It is strange, but also may hold a clue as
to why the SCP Foundation is trying to wipe

00:30:23.559 --> 00:30:25.190
out humanity.

00:30:25.190 --> 00:30:28.900
One of the soldiers recounts an event that
he witnessed before leaving the Global Occult

00:30:28.900 --> 00:30:31.929
Coalition’s headquarters at Ganzir.

00:30:31.929 --> 00:30:36.170
They had just captured an SCP soldier trying
to break into the base.

00:30:36.170 --> 00:30:39.340
The infiltrator's name was Samuel Ross.

00:30:39.340 --> 00:30:42.429
He had been strapped into an interrogation
chair and questioned.

00:30:42.429 --> 00:30:47.630
The interviewers were not getting anywhere
until Ross was threatened with torture, to

00:30:47.630 --> 00:30:50.380
which he responded “Do what you want.

00:30:50.380 --> 00:30:55.299
Once you realize you're not supposed to feel
pain, there's nothing to be afraid of anymore.”

00:30:55.299 --> 00:30:58.840
Pietro sits up straight and starts to listen
more intently.

00:30:58.840 --> 00:31:04.220
He remembers stumbling across SCP soldiers
on his way to Site-19 that exhibited the same

00:31:04.220 --> 00:31:09.030
“no pain” mentality that this Samuel Ross
seems to have.

00:31:09.030 --> 00:31:12.880
After that odd statement by Samuel Ross there
was the sound of wind.

00:31:12.880 --> 00:31:17.400
It started slow at first, then ramped up until
it was howling like a hurricane.

00:31:17.400 --> 00:31:19.809
That’s when the screaming started.

00:31:19.809 --> 00:31:22.890
The screams became louder and climbed to a
higher pitch.

00:31:22.890 --> 00:31:25.390
Then the room went dead silent.

00:31:25.390 --> 00:31:42.360
The last thing that Samuel Ross said was,
“I really liked you guys, so I was trying

00:31:42.360 --> 00:31:44.039
to be nice.

00:31:44.039 --> 00:31:47.120
We're so kind to you, you know.

00:31:47.120 --> 00:31:55.720
We fight in the light so you can die in the
dark.”

00:31:55.720 --> 00:31:59.240
Pietro sits back on his haunches and rocks
back and forth.

00:31:59.240 --> 00:32:03.150
He has an ominous feeling that there is a
connection between the missing pain of the

00:32:03.150 --> 00:32:09.090
SCP soldiers, and the reason why the Foundation
declared war on humanity.

00:32:09.090 --> 00:32:11.820
The soldier who told the story of Samual Ross
stands up.

00:32:11.820 --> 00:32:16.500
“After that interview is when the destruction
of Ganzir started from the inside.

00:32:16.500 --> 00:32:19.400
It is why the Global Occult Coalition is no
more.

00:32:19.400 --> 00:32:20.809
God help us all.”

00:32:20.809 --> 00:32:25.530
The soldier, finished with his story, turns
from the others and starts to walk away.

00:32:25.530 --> 00:32:29.950
As the soldier makes his way towards the woods
Pietro can just barely make out that he’s

00:32:29.950 --> 00:32:34.350
taken his pistol from its holster before he
disappears into the darkness.

00:32:34.350 --> 00:32:36.790
The world truly has gone mad.

00:32:36.790 --> 00:32:39.910
Pietro opens the briefcase and blacks out.

00:32:39.910 --> 00:32:42.650
Pietro sluggishly continues his walk.

00:32:42.650 --> 00:32:46.679
He’s moving down a rocky path in the middle
of the forest and his will to keep going is

00:32:46.679 --> 00:32:49.040
slowly being drained.

00:32:49.040 --> 00:32:54.059
The only reason he has not sat down and given
up is because of the driving urge to get the

00:32:54.059 --> 00:32:56.400
briefcase to 579.

00:32:56.400 --> 00:33:01.250
He wants so badly to concentrate and discover
the reason that the Foundation released the

00:33:01.250 --> 00:33:07.010
SCPs on humanity, but the need to reach 579
won’t let him to focus on anything else.

00:33:07.010 --> 00:33:11.929
He’s noticed though that every time he opens
the briefcase to skip ahead, he makes less

00:33:11.929 --> 00:33:13.580
and less progress.

00:33:13.580 --> 00:33:17.840
The warm feeling of the first few transports
has been replaced by a nauseated headache

00:33:17.840 --> 00:33:20.150
every time he comes out of the trance.

00:33:20.150 --> 00:33:22.900
Pietro exits the forest into an open field.

00:33:22.900 --> 00:33:28.030
The wind blows across the high grass looking
like green waves, and standing scattered throughout

00:33:28.030 --> 00:33:30.110
the field are statues.

00:33:30.110 --> 00:33:36.680
As Pietro approaches, he sees that they are
statues of Mobile Task Force Foundation soldiers.

00:33:36.680 --> 00:33:39.900
He slowly walks closer to the white marble
statues.

00:33:39.900 --> 00:33:44.690
He reaches the first one and looks at the
face of the frozen soldier, his eyes have

00:33:44.690 --> 00:33:50.570
been scooped out, all that remains are black,
empty, sockets.

00:33:50.570 --> 00:33:55.460
The arms of the soldier have been carved into
blades, like a praying mantis.

00:33:55.460 --> 00:33:59.980
He walks past the first statue and proceeds
to the next one when he hears something move

00:33:59.980 --> 00:34:01.970
in the grass behind him.

00:34:01.970 --> 00:34:04.090
He spins around to look at the statue.

00:34:04.090 --> 00:34:06.620
He could have swore it was in a slightly different
position.

00:34:06.620 --> 00:34:10.290
No, that’s crazy, Pietro thinks.

00:34:10.290 --> 00:34:12.530
He continues to the next statue.

00:34:12.530 --> 00:34:17.520
It is another carving of a MTF soldier, no
eyes, blades for arms.

00:34:17.520 --> 00:34:21.260
“This is really creepy,” Pietro says aloud.

00:34:21.260 --> 00:34:23.090
He proceeds through the field.

00:34:23.090 --> 00:34:27.129
He walks up a slight hill and turns around
to look at the field of statues.

00:34:27.129 --> 00:34:29.429
What he sees is terrifying.

00:34:29.429 --> 00:34:33.730
The statues have all moved and are now in
different positions.

00:34:33.730 --> 00:34:39.340
It appears as if they were slashing through
the area looking for something… or someone.

00:34:39.340 --> 00:34:43.040
Pietro continues over the hill and comes upon
a group of refugees.

00:34:43.040 --> 00:34:46.240
They are picking through the field looking
for food to eat.

00:34:46.240 --> 00:34:51.340
A fog begins to move in, it is being swept
across the meadow by the wind.

00:34:51.340 --> 00:34:56.010
Pietro watches from a distance as the fog
envelopes the small group.

00:34:56.010 --> 00:35:00.010
Suddenly there is screaming and the sound
of blades going through flesh.

00:35:00.010 --> 00:35:02.360
The screams cease almost immediately.

00:35:02.360 --> 00:35:05.180
Pietro runs down the hill to where the refugees
were.

00:35:05.180 --> 00:35:06.560
The fog lifts.

00:35:06.560 --> 00:35:10.150
The group of people have been cut to pieces.

00:35:10.150 --> 00:35:14.030
Standing in the middle of the carnage is one
of the MTF soldier statues, blood dripping

00:35:14.030 --> 00:35:16.370
from its blade arms.

00:35:16.370 --> 00:35:19.510
Pietro knows what to do… he runs.

00:35:19.510 --> 00:35:23.270
After a few miles Pietro slows to catch his
breath.

00:35:23.270 --> 00:35:27.170
“Those statues must have been created by
the Foundation” he thinks, “It’s as

00:35:27.170 --> 00:35:31.349
if they are frozen in place, but as soon as
you take your eyes off them they can move

00:35:31.349 --> 00:35:33.660
with killer speed.

00:35:33.660 --> 00:35:38.280
Even in the suit my eyesight can stop them…
but they can’t see me… they must know

00:35:38.280 --> 00:35:40.200
I’m there though since they can’t move.”

00:35:40.200 --> 00:35:45.290
Pietro Wilson opens the briefcase one again,
for what he didn’t know would be the last

00:35:45.290 --> 00:35:46.290
time.

00:35:46.290 --> 00:35:49.369
When he comes to this time he is near Site-62c.

00:35:49.369 --> 00:35:53.960
He can feel himself being pulled stronger
than ever in the direction of his destination.

00:35:53.960 --> 00:35:59.119
He walks down a deserted road past the husks
of burnt vehicles and at the end is the gate

00:35:59.119 --> 00:36:01.400
to Site-62c.

00:36:01.400 --> 00:36:03.770
There are no guards or security of any kind.

00:36:03.770 --> 00:36:08.380
It looks like the site has been abandoned
for a long time and the gate is wide open,

00:36:08.380 --> 00:36:15.940
beckoning Pietro Wilson into Site-62c... where
SCP-579 waits.

00:36:15.940 --> 00:36:22.410
Pietro Wilson enters the dark hallway he somehow
knows leads down into the crypt of Site-62c.

00:36:22.410 --> 00:36:26.980
The walls drip with what he hopes is water
from leaking pipes, but it has a metallic

00:36:26.980 --> 00:36:31.730
smell, and is much too red to actually be
water.

00:36:31.730 --> 00:36:33.210
He begins to feel nauseous.

00:36:33.210 --> 00:36:35.349
It gets harder to breathe.

00:36:35.349 --> 00:36:38.930
Even the SCP-5000 suit can’t keep him calm.

00:36:38.930 --> 00:36:41.320
He turns and runs back up the stairs out of
Site-62c.

00:36:41.320 --> 00:36:42.320
He stops a few feet from the entryway, bends
over, and vomits.

00:36:42.320 --> 00:36:47.310
Pietro begins to sob uncontrollably as the
memories of everything that has happened over

00:36:47.310 --> 00:36:51.369
the past several months suffocates his will
to go on.

00:36:51.369 --> 00:36:57.040
Then, as if an invisible force that refuses
to let him go takes control.

00:36:57.040 --> 00:37:00.650
Pietro feels as if a gun has been shoved into
the small of his back.

00:37:00.650 --> 00:37:06.800
He is being sent back into Site-62c whether
he wants to go or not.

00:37:06.800 --> 00:37:11.290
He is unsure if what is forcing him back into
the base is inside the briefcase, his own

00:37:11.290 --> 00:37:17.230
uncontrollable urge to know what is going
on, or SCP-579 itself, but he cannot stop

00:37:17.230 --> 00:37:22.140
himself from re-entering the doorway and preceding
into Site-62c.

00:37:22.140 --> 00:37:27.590
He doesn’t know what SCP-579 looks like,
but Pietro has a sinister feeling that it

00:37:27.590 --> 00:37:28.900
is watching him.

00:37:28.900 --> 00:37:32.590
He reaches the bottom of the stairway and
proceeds down a dark hallway.

00:37:32.590 --> 00:37:38.060
The power went out long ago and the only light
in the depths of Site-62c is the dim glow

00:37:38.060 --> 00:37:41.869
coming from the helmet of the SCP-5000 suit.

00:37:41.869 --> 00:37:47.170
Pietro notices long gashes along the concrete
walls, as if someone took a giant knife and

00:37:47.170 --> 00:37:49.950
dragged it from one end of the hallway to
the other.

00:37:49.950 --> 00:37:53.250
There is something at the end of the corridor
that Pietro can’t make out.

00:37:53.250 --> 00:37:57.700
As he gets closer the lights on the SCP-5000
suit begin to flicker.

00:37:57.700 --> 00:38:01.860
The thing at the end of the hallway seems
to move slightly each time the lights on the

00:38:01.860 --> 00:38:03.540
suit dim.

00:38:03.540 --> 00:38:09.599
The lights of the suit go out completely and
the entire hallway is plunged into darkness.

00:38:09.599 --> 00:38:14.300
Only for a second though, and when the lights
come back on a statue of a MTF soldier looms

00:38:14.300 --> 00:38:20.160
over Pietro, its eyes are empty sockets, its
lips are turned up in a snarl, the arms have

00:38:20.160 --> 00:38:22.310
been filed into blades.

00:38:22.310 --> 00:38:23.310
“No!”

00:38:23.310 --> 00:38:24.410
Pietro screams.

00:38:24.410 --> 00:38:28.510
He dodges around the statue, the moment it
is out of his sight he hears the sound of

00:38:28.510 --> 00:38:33.170
blades on concrete, as the statue of the soldier
comes to life and begins slashing its way

00:38:33.170 --> 00:38:34.170
down the hallway.

00:38:34.170 --> 00:38:37.810
It cannot see Pietro, but it knows he is there.

00:38:37.810 --> 00:38:41.850
It slashes all around, trying to connect with
whoever is there with it.

00:38:41.850 --> 00:38:45.150
Pietro runs to the end of the hallway and
reaches a door.

00:38:45.150 --> 00:38:49.570
He presses against the heavy metal door open,
straining against its weight all while the

00:38:49.570 --> 00:38:54.140
blind statue is still slashing, coming closer
and closer.

00:38:54.140 --> 00:38:59.280
The door is almost open, but then Pietro feels
a blade lacerate the back of the suit, cutting

00:38:59.280 --> 00:39:04.330
deeply into the skin of his back, missing
his spinal cord by millimeters.

00:39:04.330 --> 00:39:07.720
Another blade enters through the back of his
shoulder piercing straight through.

00:39:07.720 --> 00:39:11.550
He somehow pulls himself through the cracked
doorway and kicks the metal door shut behind

00:39:11.550 --> 00:39:12.550
him.

00:39:12.550 --> 00:39:15.960
He can hear the banging and scraping of blades
outside of the metal door.

00:39:15.960 --> 00:39:19.560
The creature has not given up and is trying
to break in.

00:39:19.560 --> 00:39:25.580
Pietro turns around to see he is in an observation
chamber full of instruments and screens.

00:39:25.580 --> 00:39:28.710
Blood runs down his back from the wounds inflicted
by the statue.

00:39:28.710 --> 00:39:33.470
He walks slowly over to the window, on the
desk in front of him is a file labeled SCP-579.

00:39:33.470 --> 00:39:39.430
He looks through the observation glass and
down into the chamber below.

00:39:39.430 --> 00:39:45.390
It is too dark to make anything out, but Pietro
can feel that SCP-579 is down there looking

00:39:45.390 --> 00:39:46.400
up at him.

00:39:46.400 --> 00:39:49.359
Pietro looks to his left and sees a hole in
the floor.

00:39:49.359 --> 00:39:51.070
He walks over and looks down.

00:39:51.070 --> 00:39:54.850
It leads right into the containment chamber
of 579.

00:39:54.850 --> 00:39:58.340
“Let’s get this over with,” Pietro says
out loud.

00:39:58.340 --> 00:40:01.630
He holds the briefcase over the hole and tries
to open his hand.

00:40:01.630 --> 00:40:04.250
His finger won’t budge.

00:40:04.250 --> 00:40:07.330
SCP-579 wants him to hand deliver the briefcase..

00:40:07.330 --> 00:40:12.640
Pietro Wilson takes a deep breath, closes
his eyes, and steps into the opening of the

00:40:12.640 --> 00:40:13.640
hole.

00:40:13.640 --> 00:40:14.640
He falls.

00:40:14.640 --> 00:40:20.119
In the moments before he lands in SCP-579’s
containment chamber something comes to him.

00:40:20.119 --> 00:40:24.160
He realizes that he isn’t going to be a
hero, he isn’t going to figure out why the

00:40:24.160 --> 00:40:30.400
SCP Foundation is trying to wipe out humanity…
and he isn’t going to survive.

00:40:30.400 --> 00:40:32.060
He lands hard on the ground below.

00:40:32.060 --> 00:40:36.960
It is completely dark, except for a shadow
that moves in the corner of the containment

00:40:36.960 --> 00:40:37.960
chamber.

00:40:37.960 --> 00:40:44.170
Pietro Wilson creates one last log, “if
anyone ever reads this, please, please, figure

00:40:44.170 --> 00:40:45.310
out why.

00:40:45.310 --> 00:40:47.950
Explain it to me.

00:40:47.950 --> 00:40:49.190
Someone … anyone.

00:40:49.190 --> 00:40:51.420
I don't get it.

00:40:51.420 --> 00:40:54.790
I just don't get it…”

00:40:54.790 --> 00:41:00.550
SCP-579 steps into the glow that the SCP-5000
suit is giving off.

00:41:00.550 --> 00:41:02.890
Pietro Wilson looks up at it.

00:41:02.890 --> 00:41:06.540
“Oh … so that's how it is.”

00:41:06.540 --> 00:41:16.849
he says before SCP-5000 creates its final
log: LIFE SIGNS LOST.

00:41:16.849 --> 00:41:24.670
SCP-5000 appeared in a flash of light in the
containment chamber of SCP-579 located in

00:41:24.670 --> 00:41:25.810
Site-62C.

00:41:25.810 --> 00:41:31.770
The researchers monitoring SCP-579 had no
idea where the suit came from or why it contained

00:41:31.770 --> 00:41:37.310
the body of Pietro Wilson, a foundation employee
who is assigned to Site-06 and is very much

00:41:37.310 --> 00:41:38.910
alive.

00:41:38.910 --> 00:41:44.970
Wilson appears to have no knowledge of SCP-5000
or memories of the events logged in SCP-5000’s

00:41:44.970 --> 00:41:46.190
databanks.

00:41:46.190 --> 00:41:49.640
Although the suit is believed to have been
capable at one point of a number of anomalous

00:41:49.640 --> 00:41:54.750
functions and abilities, the damage it has
sustained has rendered it inoperable except

00:41:54.750 --> 00:42:00.420
for the storage of data files, which have
now been archived and stored on secure Foundation

00:42:00.420 --> 00:42:01.970
servers.

00:42:01.970 --> 00:42:04.250
But is that really the case?

00:42:04.250 --> 00:42:10.099
The fact is, the tale of Pietro Wilson and
SCP - 5000 is one of the most complex and

00:42:10.099 --> 00:42:12.950
mysterious events in the SCP universe.

00:42:12.950 --> 00:42:17.400
You’ve got questions, and we’ve got answers
- Why Pietro?

00:42:17.400 --> 00:42:18.810
What was in the briefcase?

00:42:18.810 --> 00:42:21.350
What exactly happened at the end of the story?

00:42:21.350 --> 00:42:26.970
And perhaps most importantly of all, why did
the SCP Foundation abandon their mission,

00:42:26.970 --> 00:42:30.750
and make destroying all of humanity their
new primary directive?

00:42:30.750 --> 00:42:34.960
Whenever you’re dealing with splintered
realities and mind-melting nightmares, there’s

00:42:34.960 --> 00:42:37.670
bound to be a number of interpretations.

00:42:37.670 --> 00:42:41.040
And we’re eager to explain one of the more
popular ones right here.

00:42:41.040 --> 00:42:46.500
Soon, you’ll know it all - but to find out,
we need to start at the beginning.

00:42:46.500 --> 00:42:52.160
Our hero, Foundation employee Pietro Wilson,
was going about his day at Exclusionary Site-06.

00:42:52.160 --> 00:42:56.900
However, normal operations were interrupted
when a Mobile Task Force turned Foundation

00:42:56.900 --> 00:43:02.280
Hit Squad stormed in and began executing employees
left and right as part of their wider plan

00:43:02.280 --> 00:43:03.910
to wipe out humanity.

00:43:03.910 --> 00:43:09.700
Pietro got lucky though, and managed to find
SCP - 5000, making him undetectable to the

00:43:09.700 --> 00:43:11.690
invading MTF squad.

00:43:11.690 --> 00:43:14.750
This brings us to our first questions: Why
Pietro?

00:43:14.750 --> 00:43:19.370
And how does killing Foundation staff help
advance the O5 council’s goal of overthrowing

00:43:19.370 --> 00:43:20.370
humanity?

00:43:20.370 --> 00:43:24.310
The answer to both questions has everything
to do with the site that Pietro and his coworkers

00:43:24.310 --> 00:43:29.480
were at when the attack went down - Exclusionary
Site-06.

00:43:29.480 --> 00:43:33.210
Exclusionary Sites are a very special kind
of Foundation site that utilizes the same

00:43:33.210 --> 00:43:38.250
technology as the Scranton Box - a container
used to protect important items from reality

00:43:38.250 --> 00:43:41.930
warpers - but on a far more ambitious scale.

00:43:41.930 --> 00:43:46.060
Because of the use of this technology, these
Exclusionary Sites are essentially resistant

00:43:46.060 --> 00:43:52.020
to CK-Class Restructuring Scenarios and Temporal
Anomalies, those are where reality and or

00:43:52.020 --> 00:43:55.510
history itself are changed by a powerful entity.

00:43:55.510 --> 00:44:00.210
This makes them a perfect location for, say,
staff wanting to stage a revolt when their

00:44:00.210 --> 00:44:02.980
leaders have decided to wipe out humanity.

00:44:02.980 --> 00:44:08.060
The Foundation wished to eliminate the personnel
stationed at these protected sites as a precautionary

00:44:08.060 --> 00:44:11.990
measure, before moving onto the main phase
of their plan.

00:44:11.990 --> 00:44:16.760
But this attack was just one part of the Foundation’s
wider scheme to purge their ranks of dissenters

00:44:16.760 --> 00:44:19.589
before putting their final mission into place.

00:44:19.589 --> 00:44:23.490
In order to make sure there were no internal
threats left who could pose a threat to the

00:44:23.490 --> 00:44:28.630
new main directive, the Foundation murdered
all the staff at Exclusionary Sites, hunted

00:44:28.630 --> 00:44:33.839
down and assassinated any resigned employees,
and killed off any humanoid or human-sympathetic

00:44:33.839 --> 00:44:37.530
SCPs, leaving no one who could stop them.

00:44:37.530 --> 00:44:40.230
Or at least they thought there was no one
left…

00:44:40.230 --> 00:44:45.040
While all of this was happening, Pietro suited
up and exited the site.

00:44:45.040 --> 00:44:47.230
So, why Pietro?

00:44:47.230 --> 00:44:50.380
Because he got lucky, and he happened to stumble
upon SCP - 5000.

00:44:50.380 --> 00:44:56.570
He wasn’t the Chosen One, nor was he in
any way exceptional, beyond his willingness

00:44:56.570 --> 00:45:00.070
to see his quest for answers through to the
bitter end.

00:45:00.070 --> 00:45:04.210
Pietro really could have been any of us if
we were in his situation.

00:45:04.210 --> 00:45:07.850
When Pietro escaped, he found the world in
disarray.

00:45:07.850 --> 00:45:13.890
SCPs had been released on a global scale - destroying
infrastructure, massacring civilians, and

00:45:13.890 --> 00:45:15.840
assassinating key political figures.

00:45:15.840 --> 00:45:22.210
The Foundation had even gone public, for the
first time ever, with their new intentions:

00:45:22.210 --> 00:45:24.250
Destroy all humans.

00:45:24.250 --> 00:45:28.660
Pietro decided to head to Site-19 and get
to the bottom of their madness.

00:45:28.660 --> 00:45:33.150
On his way there, he saw a group of Mobile
Task Force members, performing a bizarre stabbing

00:45:33.150 --> 00:45:36.700
ritual to see who among them could feel pain.

00:45:36.700 --> 00:45:39.099
Remember this, it’ll be important later.

00:45:39.099 --> 00:45:44.500
Like a lot of small moments in the story of
SCP - 5000, these are puzzle pieces that can

00:45:44.500 --> 00:45:48.650
be fit together to create the true picture
of what’s happening out of the chaos.

00:45:48.650 --> 00:45:53.690
At Site-19, among the dead-eyed Foundation
workers plotting mass killings, Pietro found

00:45:53.690 --> 00:45:56.260
a treasure trove of vital information.

00:45:56.260 --> 00:46:00.570
There he learned about the existence of Project
PNEUMA, an O5 Council-approved initiative

00:46:00.570 --> 00:46:05.720
to map out the human psychosphere - otherwise
known as the collective unconscious.

00:46:05.720 --> 00:46:10.660
He also found a redacted unanimous vote from
the O5 Council and Ethics Committee, as well

00:46:10.660 --> 00:46:15.060
as a redacted series of directives sent out
to Senior Staff and Site Directors, which

00:46:15.060 --> 00:46:17.850
caused a wave of suicides and resignations.

00:46:17.850 --> 00:46:22.700
During his search, Pietro also discovered
a second series of directives sent out to

00:46:22.700 --> 00:46:29.140
the remaining Site Directors and Senior Staff,
including the phrase “Harden your heart.”

00:46:29.140 --> 00:46:31.470
These directives are known to some as “The
Cure.”

00:46:31.470 --> 00:46:35.930
While Pietro didn’t have the context to
put all this together yet, these are more

00:46:35.930 --> 00:46:38.130
vital clues to what happened.

00:46:38.130 --> 00:46:43.200
The PNEUMA Project is what incited the Foundation’s
motivation to destroy humanity - killing off

00:46:43.200 --> 00:46:47.410
humans is actually secondary to eliminating
something hiding else that’s hiding within

00:46:47.410 --> 00:46:52.940
the human psychosphere - again that’s the
collective unconsciousness of all humans.

00:46:52.940 --> 00:46:57.960
The O5 Council and the Ethics Committee were
unanimous in their approval of this project,

00:46:57.960 --> 00:47:03.180
which was like deciding to burn down a house
to kill the inhabitant inside, except in this

00:47:03.180 --> 00:47:06.240
scenario, humanity is the house.

00:47:06.240 --> 00:47:08.730
So who or what exactly is the inhabitant?

00:47:08.730 --> 00:47:11.020
You’ll find that out soon.

00:47:11.020 --> 00:47:15.099
The next thing Pietro knew, he was sitting
half way across the country, with no memory

00:47:15.099 --> 00:47:17.150
of the previous three months.

00:47:17.150 --> 00:47:22.360
He was also carrying a briefcase with no knowledge
of what was inside except that it was“not

00:47:22.360 --> 00:47:23.360
round.”

00:47:23.360 --> 00:47:29.470
He also had a strange compulsion to deliver
the briefcase to SCP - 579, for reasons he

00:47:29.470 --> 00:47:35.130
didn’t fully understand, but he hoped that
doing so would lead him to some answers.

00:47:35.130 --> 00:47:39.079
Pietro may not have known what he was holding,
but we do.

00:47:39.079 --> 00:47:45.560
The clue here is “not round” - which is
the only confirmed fact about SCP - 055, otherwise

00:47:45.560 --> 00:47:47.490
known as The Anti-Meme.

00:47:47.490 --> 00:47:53.300
This is an SCP with the primary anomalous
property of literally being unknowable.

00:47:53.300 --> 00:47:58.180
People who observe it forget what they observed,
and have no memory of even looking at 055

00:47:58.180 --> 00:47:59.660
in the first place.

00:47:59.660 --> 00:48:03.580
This is why the briefcase was able to act
as Pietro’s personal “Skip” button.

00:48:03.580 --> 00:48:07.580
Pietro was physically covering the distance
he traveled, but every time he opened the

00:48:07.580 --> 00:48:14.140
briefcase and looked at SCP-055, he forgot
that period of time, making it seem as though

00:48:14.140 --> 00:48:16.720
he simply skipped forwards.

00:48:16.720 --> 00:48:23.270
The thing he was skipping towards, SCP - 579,
is an equally mysterious and highly dangerous

00:48:23.270 --> 00:48:26.859
SCP contained within Site-62C.

00:48:26.859 --> 00:48:32.590
Nobody even really knows what 579 is, only
that it’s an anomaly so dangerous that the

00:48:32.590 --> 00:48:36.530
entirety of Site-62C was built to contain
it.

00:48:36.530 --> 00:48:39.020
So what’s so important about bringing these
two together?

00:48:39.020 --> 00:48:44.220
That, and the vital importance of Pietro’s
final mission, will become clear very soon.

00:48:44.220 --> 00:48:49.820
Pietro continued his journey with the briefcase,
encountering more horrors and countless deaths

00:48:49.820 --> 00:48:51.170
upon the way.

00:48:51.170 --> 00:48:56.490
He finally found some solace in coming across
a group of Global Occult Coalition soldiers

00:48:56.490 --> 00:49:02.270
discussing the interrogation of a captured
member of Foundation staff named Samuel Ross.

00:49:02.270 --> 00:49:06.020
Two quotes from Ross’ enigmatic speech are
of particular interest here.

00:49:06.020 --> 00:49:11.329
The first, in response to the threat of torture,
was “Do what you want.

00:49:11.329 --> 00:49:17.300
Once you realize you're not supposed to feel
pain, there's nothing to be afraid of anymore.”

00:49:17.300 --> 00:49:21.839
The second, after witnessing the death of
his captors, was “Look what you've done

00:49:21.839 --> 00:49:22.839
to yourselves.

00:49:22.839 --> 00:49:26.130
I told you you wouldn't like it, didn't you?

00:49:26.130 --> 00:49:28.450
That's why you hear your voice.

00:49:28.450 --> 00:49:30.650
But you wanted to know so badly.

00:49:30.650 --> 00:49:35.849
I really liked you guys, so I was trying to
be nice.

00:49:35.849 --> 00:49:39.900
We're so kind to you, you know.

00:49:39.900 --> 00:49:46.190
We fight in the light so you can die in the
dark...disgusting.”

00:49:46.190 --> 00:49:50.410
Do these quotes sound a little familiar?

00:49:50.410 --> 00:49:55.890
The first because, as Pietro himself recalled,
the MTF members getting stabbed earlier also

00:49:55.890 --> 00:49:58.000
didn’t seem to feel pain.

00:49:58.000 --> 00:50:03.410
The second, because describing people as “disgusting”
is an adjective favoured by another infamous

00:50:03.410 --> 00:50:05.260
SCP...

00:50:05.260 --> 00:50:07.120
SCP-682.

00:50:07.120 --> 00:50:12.450
This brings us back to “The Cure” - the
document disseminated by the O5 Council, instructing

00:50:12.450 --> 00:50:14.660
people to “Harden Their Hearts.”

00:50:14.660 --> 00:50:18.500
Whatever the Foundation discovered in the
human psychosphere, it’s apparently the

00:50:18.500 --> 00:50:24.190
cause of all pain, and hence, when the Foundation
discovered it, they were able to train themselves

00:50:24.190 --> 00:50:25.190
out of pain.

00:50:25.190 --> 00:50:31.920
And as for the SCP - 682 reference - This
is a being that despises life, and it’s

00:50:31.920 --> 00:50:36.950
believed by some that the reason 682 holds
this belief is that it’s always known about

00:50:36.950 --> 00:50:40.760
whatever the Foundation recently discovered
through Project PNEUMA.

00:50:40.760 --> 00:50:45.290
Decrypted text logs in the Foundation files
confirm this in a documented exchange between

00:50:45.290 --> 00:50:50.230
O5-1 and Tejani, the head of the Foundation
Ethics Committee.

00:50:50.230 --> 00:50:55.000
In their conversation they confirm the existence
of The Cure - which deprived the personnel

00:50:55.000 --> 00:51:00.540
of everything from pain to empathy - being
disseminated among staff prior to the massacre,

00:51:00.540 --> 00:51:04.980
and of the Foundation’s sudden ideological
alignment with SCP - 682.

00:51:04.980 --> 00:51:13.250
And they had found something else too, referred
to simply as IT . Whatever IT was, it was

00:51:13.250 --> 00:51:16.970
the reason Foundation Command decided to wipe
out humanity.

00:51:16.970 --> 00:51:19.670
But what is IT?

00:51:19.670 --> 00:51:23.849
What could possibly be so bad it was worth
killing all of humanity?

00:51:23.849 --> 00:51:28.550
Perhaps most surprising of all is that Pietro
ran into the creature’s physical manifestation,

00:51:28.550 --> 00:51:32.849
and he barely even considered it - due to
being occupied by avoiding the attacks of

00:51:32.849 --> 00:51:35.750
the statue like, mantis-armed “Blinkers.”

00:51:35.750 --> 00:51:41.210
Pietro made an entry in his log though, describing
the strange entity and described it like “a

00:51:41.210 --> 00:51:44.970
person stretched out… like the space around
them was stretched out, and they were being

00:51:44.970 --> 00:51:46.790
stretched along with it…

00:51:46.790 --> 00:51:51.710
Their body went from the ground up to the
clouds, and their jaw swung at right angles.

00:51:51.710 --> 00:51:57.750
There were these gaps, as well, black gaps
in space around its body, like wings.”

00:51:57.750 --> 00:52:01.810
Foundation staff were fighting it, shooting
at this strange entity but their weapons had

00:52:01.810 --> 00:52:03.320
no effect.

00:52:03.320 --> 00:52:09.849
This creature, this IT, is a being that inhabits
the human psychosphere - meaning it exists

00:52:09.849 --> 00:52:15.130
within the minds of all humans on some level,
driving and manipulating them to mysterious

00:52:15.130 --> 00:52:16.190
ends.

00:52:16.190 --> 00:52:17.340
What can it do?

00:52:17.340 --> 00:52:18.520
What does it want?

00:52:18.520 --> 00:52:23.330
It seems that the only people who know are
the O5 Council and the Foundation Ethics Committee

00:52:23.330 --> 00:52:25.960
who were privy to the PNEUMA report.

00:52:25.960 --> 00:52:30.590
But whatever it was they saw, they believed
it was worth killing off all of humanity just

00:52:30.590 --> 00:52:31.920
to stop it.

00:52:31.920 --> 00:52:36.380
As indicated by the unanimous vote from the
Ethics Committee, omnicide was a more ethical

00:52:36.380 --> 00:52:39.099
choice compared to the alternative.

00:52:39.099 --> 00:52:43.920
The influence of IT was also likely what gave
Pietro the strong, subconscious desire to

00:52:43.920 --> 00:52:52.710
unite the briefcase containing SCP - 055 with
SCP - 579 - even at the cost of his own life.

00:52:52.710 --> 00:52:55.460
This brings us to our final questions:

00:52:55.460 --> 00:53:02.770
Why was it so important to unite SCP - 055
and SCP- 579, and what did this act serve

00:53:02.770 --> 00:53:04.060
to achieve?

00:53:04.060 --> 00:53:08.950
As Pietro, wounded by the Blinkers and lingering
on the edge of death, finally delivered the

00:53:08.950 --> 00:53:15.099
briefcase into 579’s containment chamber,
he acknowledged the fact that he was no hero.

00:53:15.099 --> 00:53:17.510
But that’s where Pietro was wrong.

00:53:17.510 --> 00:53:22.220
After the destruction of SCP - 2000, Pietro
was in control of one of the only remaining

00:53:22.220 --> 00:53:24.730
ways to save the world.

00:53:24.730 --> 00:53:30.230
The combination of the anomalous effects of
055 and 579, as laid out in Roget’s Proposal

00:53:30.230 --> 00:53:37.070
and the article for SCP - 2998, is the Foundation’s
ultimate trump card for preventing an XK-Class

00:53:37.070 --> 00:53:38.890
end of the world scenario.

00:53:38.890 --> 00:53:44.430
If the two are united during said scenario,
the universe resets to a time before the XK

00:53:44.430 --> 00:53:47.480
Class scenario began, and prevents it from
happening.

00:53:47.480 --> 00:53:52.310
In this case, Pietro uniting the two created
a new reality where the PNEUMA Project was

00:53:52.310 --> 00:53:58.390
never launched, and IT was never discovered
- thereby averting the apocalypse.

00:53:58.390 --> 00:54:04.500
The corpse of poor dead Pietro and the highly
damaged SCP - 5000 suit he wore were the only

00:54:04.500 --> 00:54:08.410
evidence that this alternate reality ever
existed.

00:54:08.410 --> 00:54:13.010
This means that the collaboration between
Pietro Wilson and the suit he just happened

00:54:13.010 --> 00:54:17.829
to stumble upon quite literally saved the
universe as we know it from a Foundation that

00:54:17.829 --> 00:54:19.490
had gone rogue.

00:54:19.490 --> 00:54:24.390
In this regard, he’s one of the greatest
heroes the universe has ever known, even if

00:54:24.390 --> 00:54:27.460
his actions weren’t entirely his own.

00:54:27.460 --> 00:54:33.119
After all, he got a helping hand from the
suit, and another from IT - who still lurks

00:54:33.119 --> 00:54:37.990
in all our minds, mercifully undiscovered,
to this day.

00:54:37.990 --> 00:54:42.420
What was IT’s grand plan or purpose that
triggered all the madness?

00:54:42.420 --> 00:54:47.329
Anyone who ever knew for sure resides in a
universe that no longer exists, and we can

00:54:47.329 --> 00:54:53.930
only hope that a history that never happened
is somehow unable to repeat itself in ours.

